    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116">

                <pb facs="0170" n="80" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg80"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1307</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Spencer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-17T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17, 1918,
                                10 a.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.40 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consul at Harbin telegraphs, two hundred Japanese volunteer militia participated
                    in fighting at Blagoveshchensk. Six Japanese <pb facs="0171" n="81"
                        xml:id="pg81"/> killed, twelve wounded. Their leader, a shopkeeper, proved
                    Japanese colonel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spencer</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
